{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPGQ6xNtkVDmqCFWvpDLDG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"start\" \"end\" units %lthr API step\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685\"},{\"title\":\"Configure zones based on HR max or vVO2max\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/configure-zones-based-on-hr-max-or-vvo2max/46916\"},{\"title\":\"Custom Heart Rate range planned workout\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/custom-heart-rate-range-planned-workout/72460\"},{\"title\":\"Threshold HR Run setting not reflecting in workout\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/threshold-hr-run-setting-not-reflecting-in-workout/15286\"},{\"title\":\"HR target missing from Garmin Connect workout upload\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-missing-from-garmin-connect-workout-upload/5483\"},{\"title\":\"LTHR Calculation\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/lthr-calculation/23734\"},{\"title\":\"forum.intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/using-heart-rate-zones/90516\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up the official workout_doc schema, so I can't confirm the exact `start`/`end` field names or unit codes. The results are forum posts, and they're mostly about how HR targets behave rather than the API format.\n\n- **Targets are stored as a percentage of LTHR.** A forum moderator says HR targets are sent as a percentage of LTHR so workouts stay portable between athletes, and that you need to specify the HR range in % of threshold HR. One example converts a bpm range to a percentage by dividing by the threshold: if threshold HR is 170 bpm then use 130/170 = 76%.\n- **Percent-of-max-HR is a separate option.** A reply notes it is also possible with % of maxHR (which could give a slightly wider range of bpm).\n- **Percentages can resolve to different bpm than expected.** One user reported that with LTHR at 167, a \"85-90% LTHR\" target was actually taking 90%-95%, i.e. 149-158 bpm. That report is about the workout-text input, so it may not apply to direct `workout_doc` API use.\n- **Ranges are auto-generated for absolute targets.** A thread on the API says for HR it is 1.5% as the default range, and that the range can be overridden with an `hrRange` query parameter. Use 0.0 to disable range. Whether that applies to `workout_doc` steps wasn't stated.\n- **Absolute bpm entry is hard to find.** One user asked whether custom absolute bpm targets were possible, and the answers pointed back to percentages.\n\nFor the exact `start`/`end` and unit fields, the intervals.icu API docs or a test upload with the API are the best sources. I'd also check the `workout_doc` definitions in the intervals.icu API documentation or its GitHub issues, since this search didn't return them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abd3215c-c99e-4ebe-b16f-07acdd5147b1","uuid":"fe53c6ef-7dac-4fae-b0b4-3c787a9235f3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:55:50.298Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"start\" \"end\" units %lthr API step","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0148cgKzUuXCba3ptEp86eNn","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389"